      "claim": "The direct cause of the death was the administration of B-positive blood instead of A-positive blood.",
      "evidence": "The father died after being administered the wrong blood type (B-positive) which was mislabeled as A-positive.",
      "weight": 0.8,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The error was committed by an unidentified person in the blood bank, not by the doctor or the nurse.",
      "evidence": "The problem states that 'someone working at the blood bank, whose identity cannot be determined, made an error in filling the order and labeling the unit of blood'.",
      "weight": 0.9,
      "depends_on": [2]
